1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:02,080
GOLD measures
the upper atmosphere,

2
00:00:02,080 --> 00:00:05,400
which is directly affected
by the sun and what we

3
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:07,030
call space weather.

4
00:00:07,060 --> 00:00:10,000
Scientists are working
to better be able to predict

5
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:12,400
space weather because it
directly affects

6
00:00:12,400 --> 00:00:14,100
the safety of our satellites,

7
00:00:14,100 --> 00:00:15,600
the health of our astronauts,

8
00:00:15,600 --> 00:00:16,480
and the technologies

9
00:00:16,480 --> 00:00:17,520
that we use every day

10
00:00:17,520 --> 00:00:20,133
in our life like GPS navigation.

11
00:00:20,133 --> 00:00:22,563
GOLD will be sitting
twenty two thousand miles

12
00:00:22,563 --> 00:00:23,293
above Earth,

13
00:00:23,293 --> 00:00:24,163
which means that it

14
00:00:24,163 --> 00:00:25,283
can see a whole half

15
00:00:25,283 --> 00:00:28,223
of the Earth, all
of the Western Hemisphere.

16
00:00:28,223 --> 00:00:30,803
And it will be hovering
over one particular point

17
00:00:30,803 --> 00:00:31,373
on Earth,

18
00:00:31,373 --> 00:00:34,403
watching the dynamics
of the atmosphere play out

19
00:00:34,403 --> 00:00:35,000
below.

20
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:38,000
I am excited about this mission
because GOLD will

21
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:39,050
be getting information

22
00:00:39,050 --> 00:00:40,433
about the upper atmosphere

23
00:00:40,433 --> 00:00:42,020
much faster than ever before,

24
00:00:42,020 --> 00:00:43,050
and we'll be able to look

25
00:00:43,050 --> 00:00:44,250
at effects that are more

26
00:00:44,250 --> 00:00:45,290
like the weather that we

27
00:00:45,290 --> 00:00:46,967
experience down here on Earth.

28
00:00:46,967 --> 00:00:49,742
The GOLD and ICON missions
will give scientists

29
00:00:49,742 --> 00:00:51,982
the most comprehensive
view we've ever had

30
00:00:51,982 --> 00:00:53,722
of the upper atmosphere.
